  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster, I want to preview my message exactly as HFR will render it, so that I fix formatting before sending.\n\n### Scope\n\nADR on the module (HFRParsing vs app) and output (`MessageContent` as LOT-034 produces, so the reader's HTML builder renders it). Then the renderer: BBCode text → `MessageContent`, matching HFR's rendering on the captured pairs.\n\n- Module: HFRParsing · Difficulty: difficult · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-013 (#157)\n- Absorbs: FEATURES.md FEAT-013 'new BBCode renderer — ADR needed'\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): none in legacy (no preview); reference only: ultra-hfr `HFRContent` (`BBCodeParser`, `BBCodeWriter`, MPL-2.0: ideas only, no copy)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-097-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-034 (#61, done, ezzz PR #23)\n- LOT-020 (#48, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nNothing: the capture #172 (source/render pairs) is done in #400 (`W61`, `R95c`, `R95d`); LOT-034 and LOT-020 are done. The ADR is this lot's own first deliverable.\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-013 (#157), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-152 (#242); the last lot (LOT-152 (#242)) closes #157.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nFable → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- CAP-N4 (#172): BBCode round-trip pairs: for every tag of the composer toolbar (b, i, u, strike, quote, url, img, spoiler, code, fixed, color, list…), the edit-form source and the rendered message\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] ADR merged before code (Fable), naming what is not rendered identically.\n- [ ] Differential test on every CAP-N4 (#172) pair: renderer output equals the LOT-034 normalization of HFR's rendered message.\n- [ ] Unknown tags are shown as text, never as HTML (sanitization contract of ADR 0006).\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-097-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n",
